quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  2,89,"When that Book (the Qur’an) came to them from Allah, confirming what they already had; whereas, before, they used to pray for victory against the disbelievers (through the means of the Last Prophet, Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him), and his Book, the Qur’an). But when there came to them (the Prophet) whom they had (already) recognised (through their scriptures), they denied him. May the curse of Allah be on such disbelievers."
  2,90,"Low indeed is the price for which they have bartered away their souls to deny Allah’s revelation, grudging that Allah should reveal His bounty to whom He chooses from His servants. So they have ended up with wrath upon wrath. There is a humiliating punishment for the disbelievers."
  2,91,"When it is said to them: ‘Believe in what Allah has revealed,’ they say: ‘We only believe in what was revealed to us,’ and they reject what is besides that. However, it is the truth which corroborates the scriptures they already possess. Say: ‘Then why did you kill the prophets of Allah in the past if you were true believers?’"
  2,92,"Indeed, Musa (Moses) brought you clear signs, but in his absence, you chose to worship the calf, and you committed wrong."
  2,93,"(Remember) when We took your pledge and raised the Mount (of Sinai) high above you, (declaring:) ‘Hold fast to what We have given you and listen to (Our commandment).’ They said: ‘We hear but disobey.’ So, for their disbelief, they were made to drink (the love of) the calf, which sunk deep into their hearts. Say: ‘How evil is what your (so-called) faith prompts you to do if you (actually) believe (in the Torah).’"
